{"additions":3920,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #178\n\n## What\n\nThe Projects page's board now keeps itself current while the page is shown, for one GraphQL point per check.\n\n- Every **`projects-poll-interval`** (new top-level node, default `\"30s\"`, at least `\"5s\"`) the page asks only for `ProjectV2.updatedAt` (measured cost: 1 point). Card moves and project field edits bump it even though the issues' own `updatedAt` stays put, which is why the GitHub page's free REST check (#177 / #179) cannot cover boards.\n- The board is re-fetched (~3 points over the GraphQL path) **only when it moved**. `set_board` keeps the selection, the view, lanes, table sort and roadmap scroll across the swap.\n- `Board` now carries `updated_at` from the meta query (no extra request for the first comparison); a board without one (CLI fallback path, a disk cache written before this) is re-fetched by the first probe to establish the baseline.\n- Governed like every other poll: the #168 refresh scale (idle ×6, under 20 % ×2, stopped under 5 % or with `github-auto-refresh \"off\"`), capped at 10 minutes. A rate-limited answer pauses probing with the GitHub page's 30 s → 10 min backoff; `r` or any successful board fetch clears it. Other probe errors are silent (the next probe retries).\n- Status bar: the existing `board Ns ago` plus a short green `↻ updated` after a probe-driven refresh.\n- The stale re-fetch on re-entering the page after five minutes is unchanged.\n\n## Config\n\n`projects-poll-interval \"30s\"` in `assets/default.kdl`, loader accessor + validation, merge allowlist, Config Reference (en / ja) with a CI-verified example, `github-auto-refresh` text updated, guide `views-projects` \"Auto-refresh\" section (en / ja), README (en / ja).\n\n## Fixtures / tests\n\n- `vig fixtures record` records the probe (`query-project-probe` tag) so the demo and the fixture test replay an unchanged answer and never re-fetch.\n- `a_probe_refetches_the_board_only_when_updated_at_moved`: unchanged → nothing; moved → re-fetch + notice, old board stays shown; rate-limited → paused until a fetch succeeds.\n- `a_probe_refetches_a_board_without_a_known_updated_at`.\n- The fixture integration test (own process) now runs a tick, waits for the replayed probe and asserts no re-fetch.\n- `projects_poll_interval_default_override_and_validation`, `projects_poll_interval_replaced`.\n\nDemo GIFs (GitHub issue / PR, Projects) re-recorded from the refreshed fixtures.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":49,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-09T08:23:57Z","deletions":4125,"headRefName":"feat/projects-autorefresh","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":180,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMxC3Og","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nA confirmed edge case in the probe handling can cause unnecessary repeated board refetches when the probe returns `Ok(None)`.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds an auto-refresh mechanism to the Projects page that cheaply detects board changes by polling `ProjectV2.updatedAt` (1 GraphQL point) and only re-fetches the full board when the watermark moves, including config/docs/fixtures support.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add Projects board “probe → conditional refetch” polling with quota/idle scaling, rate-limit backoff, and a brief status-bar `↻ updated` notice.\n- Introduce and validate `projects-poll-interval` config (default `30s`, min `5s`) and document it (en/ja).\n- Update fixtures and demo GIFs to include the new probe request and refreshed recorded outputs.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Implements periodic probe logic, backoff, and conditional board refetch/notice wiring. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Adds `Board.updated_at` to carry the GraphQL watermark through the app/cache. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/graphql.rs | Adds `updatedAt` to the meta query and introduces the 1-point probe query + parsing. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Exposes the probe via the projects client (GraphQL-only) and ensures CLI fallback boards have `updated_at: None`. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs | Updates cache test data to include the new `updated_at` field. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Renders the Projects `↻ updated` flash in the status bar. |\r\n| src/core/gh_fixture.rs | Adds a fixture tag for the Projects probe GraphQL query. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `projects-poll-interval` parsing, defaults, validation, and tests. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Allows `projects-poll-interval` in the merge allowlist and adds a merge test. |\r\n| src/fixtures.rs | Records the new Projects probe during fixture recording so demo/test replays don’t refetch. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds the default `projects-poll-interval \"30s\"` node with documentation comments. |\r\n| README.md | Documents Projects board probing/refetch behavior and references the new interval. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese README update describing probe-driven Projects board refresh. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Adds an “Auto-refresh” section describing probe behavior and status indicators. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese version of the Projects “Auto-refresh” documentation. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Documents `projects-poll-interval` and updates `github-auto-refresh` text to include the probe. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese config reference updates for `projects-poll-interval` and `github-auto-refresh`. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-recorded Projects demo GIF for the refreshed fixtures. |\r\n| assets/demo-github-issue.gif | Re-recorded GitHub issue demo GIF from refreshed fixtures. |\r\n| assets/demo-github-pr.gif | Re-recorded GitHub PR demo GIF from refreshed fixtures. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-probe_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out | New recorded fixture for the Projects `updatedAt` probe query. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-meta_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2.out | Fixture updated to include `projectV2.updatedAt` in the meta response. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-project-items_-f_login_td72_-F_number_2_-F_first_8.out | Refreshed Projects items fixture output (rateLimit remaining changed). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_graphql_-f_query-pr-stacks_-F_owner_td72_-F_name_vig_-F_first_50.out | Refreshed PR stacks fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/api_-i_repos_owner_repo_issues_state_all_sort_updated_direction_desc_per_page_1.out | Refreshed conditional REST response fixture (ETag/body updated). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_createdAt_parent_--limit_50.out | Refreshed issues list fixture. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/pr_list_--json_number_title_state_author_labels_headRefName_baseRefName_createdAt_reviewDecision_isDraft_--limit_50.out | Refreshed PR list fixture (now empty in the recording). |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_list_--limit_50_--json_databaseId_number_name_workflowName_status_conclusion_headBranch_event_createdAt_updatedAt_url.out | Refreshed workflow runs list fixture. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747988_--json_jobs.out | New jobs JSON fixture for a recorded workflow run. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747633_--json_jobs.out | New jobs JSON fixture for a recorded workflow run. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--json_jobs.out | New jobs JSON fixture for a recorded workflow run. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--log_--job_102388841140.out | New workflow job log fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34327747574_--log_--job_102388911539.out | New workflow job log fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34325308590_--json_jobs.out | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34324770849_--json_jobs.out | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/run_view_34324764354_--json_jobs.out | Removes an older jobs JSON fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/pr_view_179_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_reviews_labels_createdAt_reviewDecision_statusCheckRollup_additions_deletions_changedFiles.out | Removes an older PR view fixture output. |\r\n| tape/fixtures/issue_view_177_--json_number_title_state_author_body_comments_labels_createdAt.out | Removes an older issue view fixture output. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 39/49 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-09T08:28:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"235c26915a6200f3c0ecc06b2ddeb440ee34c58f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMxF3bg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-09T08:32:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b42cfb444ed193d43c0465a2e2f7ac